  "id": "coldwatersentinel",
  "neon": "#e8c878",
  "note": "THE COLDWATER SENTINEL — the city paper, and now a PERIOD building rather than a modern one.\n\nIt was a stepped modern block with a chamfered clock stage and a drum lantern, which was a\nreasonable answer to \"mid-basin, transition band\" and the wrong answer to what this building\nIS. A newspaper of this age does not rebuild its own front office; it puts its name in stone\nover the door and leaves it there. So it is the Meridian's vocabulary at a quarter of the\nMeridian's height: granite plinth, reeded deco limestone shaft, pilaster strips between five\nbays, corner piers, a deep projecting cornice, a set-back attic storey, and a stone lantern\nunder a copper ogee cap.\n\n⚠ IT IS DELIBERATELY NOT A SECOND MERIDIAN, and the differences are the whole point of putting\nthem on the same street. The Meridian is a residential ziggurat: buff stone, a verdigris\ncupola, gargoyles, setbacks all the way up, no signage of any kind. This is a four-storey\ncommercial block: it is GREY at the bottom where the Meridian is buff, it steps once rather\nthan three times, it carries gilt lettering on a frieze (a newspaper is in the business of\nhaving its name read), and its crown is a working lamp rather than an ornament. Two buildings\nof one period by two different hands, which is what a real street looks like.\n\n⚠ EVERY OFF-CENTRE BOX HERE IS SQUARE IN PLAN. `F()` rotates a box's POSITION to the entrance\nand leaves its footprint pointing north, so an off-centre box wider than it is deep reaches a\ndifferent radius at each of the four facings and `gl:mesh` fails it — the divebar false-front\nbug, which failed on three models at once. Pilasters, piers and the lantern are all square or\nradial; the only non-square box is centred, where the footprint cannot rotate out from under\nitself.\n\n⚠ THE COPPER IS ITS OWN SEGMENT, NOT A ROOF FACE. `facePals` is a code-arm facility and there\nis no authored equivalent — a segment takes ONE palette — so the cornice caps are thin boxes in\nty_verdigris sitting on the stone below them. That is also the honest construction: a stone\ncornice with a copper flashing over it is two materials, not one material with two faces.\n\nRENDER_TUNE.legacyArms puts the sentinel arm back.",
  "pal": "ty_meridian",
  "replaces": "sentinel",
